# SID 10000001 — Outbound ICMP (ping) from HOME_NET to EXTERNAL_NET
# Detects: reconnaissance / diagnostic ICMP traffic leaving the trusted network
# ATT&CK: T1016.001 - Internet Connection Discovery
#
# This is the exact rule as deployed and tested (pfSense custom.rules,
# ECORP interface). It omits the $ prefix on HOME_NET/EXTERNAL_NET and
# a rev field; pfSense's Snort build accepted it and it fired correctly
# against live test traffic (see results/test-results.md).
alert icmp HOME_NET any -> EXTERNAL_NET any (msg:"Ping detected";sid:10000001)

# Standard-practice variant (equivalent behavior, not yet re-tested):
# alert icmp $HOME_NET any -> $EXTERNAL_NET any (msg:"Ping detected"; sid:10000001; rev:1;)
